#
# QNX: graceful render-only fallback when SCREEN_PROPERTY_FD returns ENOTSUP
# on a pixmap-owned buffer. Matches the `--virgl` QEMU smoke path that hits
# the ENOTSUP error at qnx_render_producer.cc:515.
#
# The previous code unconditionally failed the entire export when the screen
# buffer did not expose a backing FD. Per screen.h:
#
#   SCREEN_PROPERTY_FD = 174
#     - "this can only be used to provide memory to Screen"
#     - "Applicable to: buffer"
#     - default privileges rw-r--r--; Configurable: No (read-only at get)
#
# The implication: pixmap buffers created by `screen_create_pixmap_buffer`
# own their memory internally and never expose a gettable FD. Returning
# ENOTSUP on `screen_get_buffer_property_iv(buf, SCREEN_PROPERTY_FD)` is the
# documented, correct behavior. The producer must accept that.
#
# This patch:
#   1. Treats ENOTSUP on SCREEN_PROPERTY_FD as the expected pixmap-buffer
#      case in `QnxRenderProducer::BuildScreenBufferDescriptor`. The function
#      continues with an invalid `out_desc->fd` (the default) and the
#      rest of the descriptor is still populated (format / stride / size /
#      native_image).
#   2. Detects that case in `QnxFrameImporter::ImportAndDisplayFrame` and
#      short-circuits the EGL image import, deferring presentation to the
#      local Screen buffer instead of attempting a cross-process dma-buf
#      share that is not supported.
#
# See docs/qnx/history/research/qnx-angle-dmabuf-export-investigation-2026-07-12/SCREEN-PROPERTY-FD-BLOCKER-2026-07-13.md
# for full investigation and reproduction logs.

--- /tmp/gen_render_only/qnx/ui/ozone/platform/qnx/qnx_render_producer.cc	2026-07-13 11:27:58.231224311 +0900
+++ ui/ozone/platform/qnx/qnx_render_producer.cc	2026-07-13 11:27:58.231224311 +0900
@@ -508,9 +508,14 @@ bool QnxRenderProducer::BuildScreenBufferDescriptor(
 
